<title>FRANCE: Algeria expanding gas unit to 7 mln tonnes a year.</title>
<headline>Algeria expanding gas unit to 7 mln tonnes a year.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria is expanding a liquefied propane gas complex to lift capacity by 2.2 million tonnes to seven million tonnes a year, the official Algerian news agency APS said on Sunday.</p>
<p>It said work, being undertaken by an unnamed Japanese firm, had started at the Bethioua plant in the western province of Oran, home of the major energy export port of Arzew.</p>
<p>APS said the work should be finished in 28 months.</p>
</text>
